@startuml
title Microwave Oven Control - State Diagram

state "Door Closed" as InitialState
state "Door Open"
state "Door Open With Item"
state "Door Shut"
state "Door Shut With Item"
state "Ready To Cook"
state Cooking
state Checking
state Alarm
state Done
state Waiting

InitialState --> DoorOpen : Door Opened
DoorOpen --> DoorShut : Door Closed
DoorOpen --> DoorShutItem : Food Placed
DoorShutItem --> ReadyToCook : Door Closed
ReadyToCook --> Cooking : Start Cooking
Cooking --> Done : Timeout or Cancel
Done --> DoorShut : Completed

Checking --> Cook : OK
Checking --> Alarm : Turntable Fault
Checking --> Alarm : Emitter Fault
Alarm --> Disabled : Issue Detected

DoorOpen --> FoodPlaced : Food Placed
FoodPlaced --> ReadyToCook : Door Closed
ReadyToCook --> Cooking : Start Cooking
Cooking --> Done : Timeout or Cancel
Done --> DoorOpen : Completed

DoorShut --> DoorOpen : Door Opened
DoorOpen --> DoorShut : Door Closed
DoorOpen --> DoorShutItem : Food Placed
DoorShutItem --> ReadyToCook : Door Closed
ReadyToCook --> Cooking : Start Cooking
Cooking --> Done : Timeout or Cancel
Done --> DoorShut : Completed

DoorOpen --> Waiting : User Input
Waiting --> DoorShut : User Input
Waiting --> Idle : Cancel
Idle --> PINEntered : PIN Entered
PINEntered --> InvalidPIN : Incorrect PIN
InvalidPIN --> Idle : Retry or Cancel
InvalidPIN --> CardRetained : Multiple Incorrect PINs
CardRetained --> Idle : User Returns Card

PINEntered --> Options : Correct PIN
Options --> WithdrawalRequest : User
WithdrawalRequest --> RejectedTransaction : Rejected
RejectedTransaction --> Idle : Return Card
WithdrawalRequest --> ApprovedTransaction : Approved
ApprovedTransaction --> DispenseCash : Dispense Cash
DispenseCash --> PrintReceipt : Print Receipt
PrintReceipt --> ReturnCard : Return Card
ReturnCard --> Idle : User Input

Idle --> OutOfCash : Out of Cash
OutOfCash --> Reset : Reset
Reset --> Idle : Ready for Next User

Case ID: case_73_oven
Complexity: medium

Requirement:
Oven — Polished Requirement Specification

Functional Requirements
1. The system shall display the current time when it is waiting for user input.
2. The system shall allow the user to choose between full power and half power levels.
3. The system shall enable the user to set cooking time by entering a number.
4. The system shall remain inactive if the door is open during operation.
5. The system shall stop immediately when the door is opened during the cooking process.
6. The system shall allow the user to cancel the cooking process.
7. The system shall return to displaying the current time after stopping or cancelling and wait for the next use.

state "Display Current Time" as DisplayCurrentTime
DoorShut --> DisplayCurrentTime : Door Closed
DisplayCurrentTime --> DoorOpen : Door Opened
DisplayCurrentTime --> Cooking : Start Cooking
Cooking --> Done : Timeout or Cancel
Done --> DisplayCurrentTime : Completed

state "Power Level Selection" as PowerLevelSelection
DoorShut --> PowerLevelSelection : Door Closed
PowerLevelSelection --> Cooking : Full Power or Half Power Selected

state "Cooking Time Input" as CookingTimeInput
PowerLevelSelection --> CookingTimeInput : Door Closed
CookingTimeInput --> ReadyToCook : Cooking Time Entered

Case ID: case_69_atm_many_scenarios_6
Complexity: medium

Requirement:
Atm Many Scenarios Scenario 6 — Polished Requirement Specification

Functional Requirements
1. The system shall check if the entered PIN is correct.
2. The system shall ask for the PIN again if it is incorrect.
3. The system shall keep the card for security reasons
@enduml
